---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import JsonSchemaGenerator from '../../components/JsonSchemaGenerator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="JSON Schema Generator"
  description="Paste a sample JSON object and instantly generate a matching JSON Schema — useful for AI function calling and API validation."
>
  <JsonSchemaGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why generate a schema from a sample</h2>
  <p>
    Writing JSON Schema by hand is tedious and error-prone, especially for
    nested objects. This is especially useful when defining function-calling
    schemas for AI models — paste an example of the output you want, and get
    a starting schema instantly.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste a representative sample of your JSON data.</li>
    <li>The tool infers types (string, number, boolean, array, object) automatically.</li>
    <li>Copy the generated schema and refine it — add constraints like enums, min/max, or patterns as needed.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Does it detect required vs optional fields?</strong> It marks
    every field present in your sample as required — since a single example
    can't tell which fields are truly optional, review and adjust manually.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Does this send my data anywhere?</strong> No — schema inference
    runs entirely in your browser.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
